    "clean_text": "Today we differentiate bimolecular SN2 reactions from unimolecular SN1 mechanisms. Pay attention to course deadlines: online pre-lab assignment five is due this evening at 8:00 PM. We also have a laboratory safety quiz scheduled for next Monday morning at 9:00 AM. Here is the key diagnostic question: why does an SN2 substitution at a chiral carbon center cause complete Walden inversion of configuration? Because backside nucleophilic attack occurs 180 degrees opposite the leaving group."
